# Design stack

## Typography + space

Fluid type and space live as **Utopia-generated CSS custom properties** in `src/styles/global.css` (viewport ~360→1240, semantic roles like `--type-brand|display|index|title|lead|body|nav|caption` and `--space-*`).

- Extend or reuse those tokens; do not invent parallel `clamp()` scales or a second type system
- Prefer semantic roles over one-off font sizes

## Layout

Hand-written CSS in `global.css` — sparse artist layouts, not a utility framework.

- **Do not** add Tailwind, Open Props, or a layout-component library unless explicitly asked
- Prefer tightening existing shells/grids over introducing a new grid system

### Shell vs bleed

Composed pages (About, CV, writing, project detail, maps, collaborations, research) use `.layout-shell` + `body--sheet`: gutter `--page-pad`, full viewport width, forced light palette. Header + footer use the same gutter.

**Bleed** (pad 0 on main): homepage and works index. Works index still gets `body--sheet` for the white palette. Full-bleed media (maps canvases, lightboxes, gallery breakouts) can still escape the shell.

### Variants

| Variant | Use |
|---|---|
| `home` | Full-bleed hero |
| `work` | Works index |
| `writing` | Sticky header + TOC |
| `page` | About, CV, project detail, maps, collaborations, research, and new composed sections |
| default | 404 |

A new composed page is `variant="page"` plus a content class. Use `.layout-split` (optional `.layout-split--tight`) for two-column sections. It stacks at **70rem**. Do not force writing’s TOC/figures grid or project intro (`1fr / 2fr`) onto `.layout-split`.

Reading width: `.measure` (`66ch`) or `.measure--lede` (`38rem`).

### Tokens (in `:root`)

| Token | Role |
|---|---|
| `--page-pad` | Outer gutter (header, footer, shell mains) |
| `--measure-prose` | Long reading (`66ch`) |
| `--measure-lede` | Short intros (`38rem`) |
| `--split-track` | Two-column track for `.layout-split` |
| `--split-gap` / `--split-gap-tight` | Split column gaps |

## Motion

See `animation.mdc` — CSS + Astro view transitions for chrome; GSAP only later for narrative project views.
